{
  "id": "task-diy-6",
  "task": 6,
  "title": "DIY 6, step by step",
  "segments": [
    {
      "example": null,
      "extra": false,
      "title": "Reverse in place, build a menu in a loop",
      "steps": [
        {
          "caption": "word points at a StringBuilder holding stressed: one object, eight characters.",
          "vars": [{"name": "word", "ref": "B"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "B", "text": "stressed", "class": "StringBuilder"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Reverse it. The builder turns its own characters back to front: the same object, now holding desserts. There is nothing new to catch.",
          "vars": [{"name": "word", "ref": "B"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "B", "text": "desserts", "class": "StringBuilder"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Print it after Reversed:.",
          "print": "Reversed: desserts\n",
          "from": {"array": "B"},
          "vars": [{"name": "word", "ref": "B"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "B", "text": "desserts", "class": "StringBuilder"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Three menu items in an array, and an empty builder for the menu.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]"},
            {"id": "M", "text": "", "class": "StringBuilder"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Round 1 of a loop from 1 to 3 appends 1, a dot and a space, the first item, and a line break. A line break is a character too: the ↵ box.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]", "highlight": [0]},
            {"id": "M", "text": "1. Start\n", "class": "StringBuilder"}
          ],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "It", "index": 0}, "to": {"array": "M"}, "text": "Start"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Round 2 appends the second item, to the same object.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]", "highlight": [1]},
            {"id": "M", "text": "1. Start\n2. Settings\n", "class": "StringBuilder"}
          ],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "It", "index": 1}, "to": {"array": "M"}, "text": "Settings"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Round 3, the last item. Still one object: the arrow never moved.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]", "highlight": [2]},
            {"id": "M", "text": "1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n", "class": "StringBuilder"}
          ],
          "flow": [{"from": {"array": "It", "index": 2}, "to": {"array": "M"}, "text": "Exit"}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Insert the heading Menu: and a line break at index 0. Everything already in the builder slides along to make room.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]"},
            {
              "id": "M",
              "text": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n",
              "class": "StringBuilder",
              "highlight": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Turn the builder into a String and print it.",
          "print": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n",
          "from": {"array": "MS"},
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "M"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]"},
            {"id": "M", "text": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n", "class": "StringBuilder"},
            {"id": "MS", "text": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n", "class": "String", "solid": true}
          ],
          "flow": [
            {"from": {"array": "M"}, "to": {"array": "MS"}, "text": "Menu: ↵ 1. Start ↵ 2. Settings ↵ 3. Exit ↵"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Change StringBuilder to StringBuffer and run it again. The same calls build the same text, so the output does not change: a StringBuffer only adds a lock, for threads.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "Bf"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]"},
            {"id": "Bf", "text": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n", "class": "StringBuffer"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Now write the code that makes this happen, run it with ▶, then press Check my output.",
          "vars": [{"name": "items", "ref": "It"}, {"name": "menu", "ref": "Bf"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "It", "values": ["\"Start\"", "\"Settings\"", "\"Exit\""], "class": "String[]"},
            {"id": "Bf", "text": "Menu:\n1. Start\n2. Settings\n3. Exit\n", "class": "StringBuffer"}
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
